###############################################################################
# Q10 -- Benchmark results
###############################################################################

# No energy/force/stress accuracy metric is reported in a form the schema captures (see Q12).

###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Table I: training time in minutes on an Intel Xeon E5-2640 (2.40 GHz)
# and prediction speed in geometries per second on a 2.8 GHz Intel Core i7
# notebook, for each of the ten models; kept as text in trainingHardware
# and inferenceHardware (minutes and geometries/s are not the units of
# mlips:trainingDuration and mlips:inferenceTimePerAtom).

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Force and energy errors of the Table I models are not printed in the parts read; no AccuracyMetric is encoded.
# - The reference level of the ten bulk data sets is not restated (they are the MD17-type trajectories of the earlier GDML/sGDML papers), so the data sets carry no reference calculation.
# - The paracetamol walk-through (geometries from a 500 K PBE+TS trajectory, labels recomputed at PBE0+MBD, MD at 300 K) is a second paracetamol model whose size and errors were not captured; it is not encoded as a separate run.
# - Kernel hyperparameters (sigma) are selected per model and not tabulated.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
